concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-23-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23(2) Decisions to be made by authorised persons"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-23-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) A decision in respect of a request made to a court, or made to a tribunal, authority or body that is specified in Schedule 1, may be made on behalf of that court, tribunal, authority or body by the principal officer of that court, tribunal, authority or body or, subject to the regulations, by an officer of that court, tribunal, authority or body acting within the scope of authority exercisable by him or her in accordance with arrangements approved by the principal officer of that court, tribunal, authority or body. 24  Power to refuse request—diversion of resources etc." ;
    skos:definition "(2) A decision in respect of a request made to a court, or made to a tribunal, authority or body that is specified in Schedule 1, may be made on behalf of that court, tribunal, authority or body by the principal officer of that court, tribunal, authority or body or, subject to the regulations, by an officer of that court, tribunal, authority or body acting within the scope of authority exercisable by him or her in accordance with arrangements approved by the principal officer of that court, tribunal, authority or body. 24  Power to refuse request—diversion of resources etc."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c3ce3ea218b987cfcee98cf0bd5bed7f9be4798eccb14526e0980fa6c0f4ad7e" ;
    values:partOf concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-23 ;
    cof:pageNumber "70"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Authorized persons can make decisions on behalf of specified courts, tribunals, authorities or bodies. Agency or Minister must consider resources for decision-making. Agency or Minister may treat multiple requests as a single request if satisfied that they relate to the same document or documents." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
