doc:sch-4-sec-23-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "23(1) Decisions to be made by authorised persons" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If an agency or Minister is satisfied, when dealing with a request for a document, that a practical refusal reason exists in relation to the request (see section 24AA), the agency or Minister: (a) must undertake a request consultation process (see section 24AB); and (b) if, after the request consultation process, the agency or Minister is satisfied that the practical refusal reason still exists—the agency or Minister may refuse to give access to the document in accordance with the request." ;
    cof:pageNumber "70"^^xsd:integer .

concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-23-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "23(2) Decisions to be made by authorised persons"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-23-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) For the purposes of this section, the agency or Minister may treat 2 or more requests as a single request if the agency or Minister is satisfied that: (a) the requests relate to the same document or documents; or   Access to documents  Part III  Section 24AA Freedom of Information Act 1982 Compilation date: 01/01/2026 (b) the requests relate to documents, the subject matter of which is substantially the same. 24AA  When does a practical refusal reason exist?" ;
    skos:definition "(2) For the purposes of this section, the agency or Minister may treat 2 or more requests as a single request if the agency or Minister is satisfied that: (a) the requests relate to the same document or documents; or   Access to documents  Part III  Section 24AA Freedom of Information Act 1982 Compilation date: 01/01/2026 (b) the requests relate to documents, the subject matter of which is substantially the same. 24AA  When does a practical refusal reason exist?"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fdb17c29fcaece9435c14fb32a6a47ab9022fc5f42762660806eb7037fb71865" ;
    values:partOf concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-23 ;
    cof:pageNumber "70"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Authorized persons can make decisions on behalf of specified courts, tribunals, authorities or bodies. Agency or Minister must consider resources for decision-making. Agency or Minister may treat multiple requests as a single request if satisfied that they relate to the same document or documents." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf> ;
    dc:source "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.70" ;
    cml:asserts concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-23-ss-2-norm .
