    skos:definition "(2) An agency may refuse a request for access to a document if: (a) in order to comply with section 6C, the agency has taken contractual measures to ensure that it receives the document; and (b) the agency has not received the document; and (c) the agency has taken all reasonable steps to receive the document in accordance with those contractual measures."@en ;
