concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-29 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "29 Charges"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-29 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Where, under the regulations, an agency or Minister decides that an applicant is liable to pay a charge in respect of a request for access to a document, or the provision of access to a document, the agency or Minister must give to the applicant a written notice stating: (a) that the applicant is liable to pay a charge; and (b) the agency’s or Minister’s preliminary assessment of the amount of the charge, and the basis on which the assessment is made; and (c) that the applicant may contend that the charge has been wrongly assessed, or should be reduced or not imposed; and" ;
    skos:definition "(1) Where, under the regulations, an agency or Minister decides that an applicant is liable to pay a charge in respect of a request for access to a document, or the provision of access to a document, the agency or Minister must give to the applicant a written notice stating: (a) that the applicant is liable to pay a charge; and (b) the agency’s or Minister’s preliminary assessment of the amount of the charge, and the basis on which the assessment is made; and (c) that the applicant may contend that the charge has been wrongly assessed, or should be reduced or not imposed; and"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "04f383b8341754280c2ba8af98945f785f864f201b7dbe2af5e6938a277ed178" ;
    cof:pageNumber "83"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Agency or Minister must give written notice to applicant stating they are liable to pay a charge." ;
    dc:description "written notice stating the applicant is liable to pay a charge, preliminary assessment of the amount of the charge, and basis for the assessment" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf> ;
    dc:source "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.83" ;
    cml:asserts concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-29-norm .
