concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-37-ss-2a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "37(2A) Documents affecting enforcement of law and protection of public"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-37-ss-2a ;
    values:originalText "(2A) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b), a person is taken to be a confidential source of information in relation to the enforcement or administration of the law if the person is receiving, or has received, protection under a program conducted under the auspices of the Australian Federal Police, or the police force of a State or Territory, for the protection of: (a) witnesses; or (b) people who, because of their relationship to, or association with, a witness need, or may need, such protection; or (c) any other people who, for any other reason, need or may need, such protection." ;
    skos:definition "(2A) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b), a person is taken to be a confidential source of information in relation to the enforcement or administration of the law if the person is receiving, or has received, protection under a program conducted under the auspices of the Australian Federal Police, or the police force of a State or Territory, for the protection of: (a) witnesses; or (b) people who, because of their relationship to, or association with, a witness need, or may need, such protection; or (c) any other people who, for any other reason, need or may need, such protection."@en ;
