concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47e a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "47E Public interest conditional exemptions—certain operations of"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-47e ;
    values:originalText "agencies A document is conditionally exempt if its disclosure under this Act would, or could reasonably be expected to, do any of the following: (a) prejudice the effectiveness of procedures or methods for the conduct of tests, examinations or audits by an agency; (b) prejudice the attainment of the objects of particular tests, examinations or audits conducted or to be conducted by an agency; (c) have a substantial adverse effect on the management or assessment of personnel by the Commonwealth or by an agency; (d) have a substantial adverse effect on the proper and efficient conduct of the operations of an agency. Note: Access must generally be given to a conditionally exempt document unless it would be contrary to the public interest (see section 11A)." ;
    skos:definition "agencies A document is conditionally exempt if its disclosure under this Act would, or could reasonably be expected to, do any of the following: (a) prejudice the effectiveness of procedures or methods for the conduct of tests, examinations or audits by an agency; (b) prejudice the attainment of the objects of particular tests, examinations or audits conducted or to be conducted by an agency; (c) have a substantial adverse effect on the management or assessment of personnel by the Commonwealth or by an agency; (d) have a substantial adverse effect on the proper and efficient conduct of the operations of an agency. Note: Access must generally be given to a conditionally exempt document unless it would be contrary to the public interest (see section 11A)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d99fd961cd90c24fbe6c58c870603462a8d3778639b34ded825ac1a10fc3f35f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "103"^^xsd:integer ;
