doc:sch-4-sec-47e a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "47E Public interest conditional exemptions—certain operations of" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "agencies A document is conditionally exempt if its disclosure under this Act would, or could reasonably be expected to, do any of the following: (a) prejudice the effectiveness of procedures or methods for the conduct of tests, examinations or audits by an agency; (b) prejudice the attainment of the objects of particular tests, examinations or audits conducted or to be conducted by an agency; (c) have a substantial adverse effect on the management or assessment of personnel by the Commonwealth or by an agency; (d) have a substantial adverse effect on the proper and efficient conduct of the operations of an agency. Note: Access must generally be given to a conditionally exempt document unless it would be contrary to the public interest (see section 11A)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "103"^^xsd:integer .

concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47f a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "47F Public interest conditional exemptions—personal privacy"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-47f ;
    values:originalText "General rule (1) A document is conditionally exempt if its disclosure under this Act would involve the unreasonable disclosure of personal information about any person (including a deceased person). (2) In determining whether the disclosure of the document would involve the unreasonable disclosure of personal information, an agency or Minister must have regard to the following matters: (a) the extent to which the information is well known; (b) whether the person to whom the information relates is known to be (or to have been) associated with the matters dealt with in the document; (c) the availability of the information from publicly accessible sources;" ;
    skos:definition "General rule (1) A document is conditionally exempt if its disclosure under this Act would involve the unreasonable disclosure of personal information about any person (including a deceased person). (2) In determining whether the disclosure of the document would involve the unreasonable disclosure of personal information, an agency or Minister must have regard to the following matters: (a) the extent to which the information is well known; (b) whether the person to whom the information relates is known to be (or to have been) associated with the matters dealt with in the document; (c) the availability of the information from publicly accessible sources;"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "48352168b5d297ea082d1f1ace5c17c0ffa85fb95702d14f7b0c7a135660bfd7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "103"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47f-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47f-ss-2 ;
