doc:sch-4-sec-47j-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "47J(1) Public interest conditional exemptions—the economy" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A document is conditionally exempt if its disclosure under this Act would, or could be reasonably expected to, have a substantial adverse effect on Australia’s economy by: (a) influencing a decision or action of a person or entity; or (b) giving a person (or class of persons) an undue benefit or detriment, in relation to business carried on by the person (or class), by providing premature knowledge of proposed or possible action or inaction of a person or entity. Note: A person includes a body corporate and a body politic (see subsection 2C(1) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901). Examples of a body politic include the government of the Commonwealth, a State, a Territory or a foreign country." ;
    cof:pageNumber "107"^^xsd:integer .

concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47j-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "47J(2) Public interest conditional exemptions—the economy"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-47j-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), a substantial adverse effect on Australia’s economy includes a substantial adverse effect on: (a) a particular sector of the economy; or (b) the economy of a particular region of Australia." ;
    skos:definition "(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), a substantial adverse effect on Australia’s economy includes a substantial adverse effect on: (a) a particular sector of the economy; or (b) the economy of a particular region of Australia."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7fa8c6c74dfdf138c83b85d433285771d13a343a9f32b5d5b2274f237e476d1f" ;
    values:partOf concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-47j ;
    cof:pageNumber "107"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "A substantial adverse effect on Australia's economy includes a substantial adverse effect on a particular sector of the economy or the economy of a particular region of Australia." ;
