doc:sch-4-sec-54k a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "54K Key concepts—what is an IC reviewable decision?" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "An IC reviewable decision is: (a) a decision covered by subsection 54L(2) (access refusal decisions); or (b) a decision covered by subsection 54M(2) (access grant decisions). Note: IC reviewable decision is short for Information Commissioner reviewable decision.   Review by Information Commissioner  Part VII IC reviewable decisions  Division 3 Section 54L Freedom of Information Act 1982 Compilation date: 01/01/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "128"^^xsd:integer .

concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54l a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "54L IC reviewable decisions—access refusal decisions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-54l ;
    values:originalText "(1) An application may be made to the Information Commissioner for a review of a decision covered by subsection (2). (2) This subsection covers the following decisions: (a) an access refusal decision; (b) a decision made by an agency on internal review of an access refusal decision (see section 54C); (c) a decision refusing to allow a further period for making an application for internal review of an access refusal decision (under section 54B). Note 1: An application for the review of an access refusal decision made for the purposes of paragraph (a) may be made regardless of whether the decision was the subject of internal review. Note 2: If no decision is made on internal review within 30 days, a decision to affirm the original access refusal decision is taken to have been made (see section 54D). (3) The IC review application may be made by, or on behalf of, the person who made the request to which the decision relates." ;
    skos:definition "(1) An application may be made to the Information Commissioner for a review of a decision covered by subsection (2). (2) This subsection covers the following decisions: (a) an access refusal decision; (b) a decision made by an agency on internal review of an access refusal decision (see section 54C); (c) a decision refusing to allow a further period for making an application for internal review of an access refusal decision (under section 54B). Note 1: An application for the review of an access refusal decision made for the purposes of paragraph (a) may be made regardless of whether the decision was the subject of internal review. Note 2: If no decision is made on internal review within 30 days, a decision to affirm the original access refusal decision is taken to have been made (see section 54D). (3) The IC review application may be made by, or on behalf of, the person who made the request to which the decision relates."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ac73b9cbb7aaecc29612b47216f3c523d70a4479e7fe990d1543c1b7e721f60c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "129"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54l-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-54l-ss-2 ;
