    values:originalText "(2) The agency or Minister must, as soon as practicable, take all reasonable steps to notify the affected third party for the document of the application. Note 1: For affected third party, see section 53C. Note 2: The agency or Minister is not required to give notice if the Information Commissioner orders that it is not appropriate to do so in the circumstances (see section 54Q)." ;
    skos:definition "(2) The agency or Minister must, as soon as practicable, take all reasonable steps to notify the affected third party for the document of the application. Note 1: For affected third party, see section 53C. Note 2: The agency or Minister is not required to give notice if the Information Commissioner orders that it is not appropriate to do so in the circumstances (see section 54Q)."@en ;
