concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55h-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "55H(5) Procedure in IC review—reference of questions of law to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-55h-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) If a question of law is referred, the Information Commissioner must not, for the purposes of the IC review: (a) give a decision to which the question is relevant before the Federal Court of Australia makes a decision in relation to the reference; or (b) proceed in a manner, or make a decision, that is inconsistent with the opinion of the Federal Court of Australia on the question." ;
    skos:definition "(5) If a question of law is referred, the Information Commissioner must not, for the purposes of the IC review: (a) give a decision to which the question is relevant before the Federal Court of Australia makes a decision in relation to the reference; or (b) proceed in a manner, or make a decision, that is inconsistent with the opinion of the Federal Court of Australia on the question."@en ;
