concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55q a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "55Q Decision on IC review—correction of errors"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-55q ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Information Commissioner may correct an obvious error in a decision under section 55K of the Information Commissioner on an IC review. Example: The following are examples of obvious errors: (a) an obvious clerical or typographical error in the text of the decision or statement of reasons; (b) an inconsistency between the decision and the statement of reasons. (2) The Information Commissioner may correct an obvious error: (a) on an application by a review party; or (b) on the Information Commissioner’s initiative.   Review by Information Commissioner  Part VII Information gathering powers  Division 8 Section 55R Freedom of Information Act 1982 Compilation date: 01/01/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Information Commissioner may correct an obvious error in a decision under section 55K of the Information Commissioner on an IC review. Example: The following are examples of obvious errors: (a) an obvious clerical or typographical error in the text of the decision or statement of reasons; (b) an inconsistency between the decision and the statement of reasons. (2) The Information Commissioner may correct an obvious error: (a) on an application by a review party; or (b) on the Information Commissioner’s initiative.   Review by Information Commissioner  Part VII Information gathering powers  Division 8 Section 55R Freedom of Information Act 1982 Compilation date: 01/01/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ec07180150e5118f21f6dbdabe5be450a23fb20ac3240c8a636f93c13799d1dd" ;
