concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55x a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "55X Information gathering powers—administration of oath or"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-55x ;
    values:originalText "affirmation (1) If, by a notice under subsection 55W(1), the Information Commissioner requires a person to appear before him or her, the Information Commissioner may: (a) administer an oath or affirmation to the person; and (b) examine the person on oath or affirmation. (2) The oath or affirmation to be taken or made by a person for the purposes of this section is an oath or affirmation that the answers the person will give will be true. (3) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person is required under this section to be examined on oath or affirmation; and (b) the person engages in conduct; and (c) the person’s conduct breaches that requirement. Penalty for a contravention of this subsection: 6 months imprisonment. Note: Chapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of criminal responsibility." ;
    skos:definition "affirmation (1) If, by a notice under subsection 55W(1), the Information Commissioner requires a person to appear before him or her, the Information Commissioner may: (a) administer an oath or affirmation to the person; and (b) examine the person on oath or affirmation. (2) The oath or affirmation to be taken or made by a person for the purposes of this section is an oath or affirmation that the answers the person will give will be true. (3) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person is required under this section to be examined on oath or affirmation; and (b) the person engages in conduct; and (c) the person’s conduct breaches that requirement. Penalty for a contravention of this subsection: 6 months imprisonment. Note: Chapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of criminal responsibility."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a69ad33c292fe18441e94306be54fc9a52e27fb2686932199c0b719fa2d803b2" ;
    cof:pageNumber "156"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55x-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55x-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55x-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf> ;
    dc:source "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.156" .
doc:sch-4-sec-55x a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "55X Information gathering powers—administration of oath or" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "affirmation (1) If, by a notice under subsection 55W(1), the Information Commissioner requires a person to appear before him or her, the Information Commissioner may: (a) administer an oath or affirmation to the person; and (b) examine the person on oath or affirmation. (2) The oath or affirmation to be taken or made by a person for the purposes of this section is an oath or affirmation that the answers the person will give will be true. (3) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person is required under this section to be examined on oath or affirmation; and (b) the person engages in conduct; and (c) the person’s conduct breaches that requirement. Penalty for a contravention of this subsection: 6 months imprisonment. Note: Chapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of criminal responsibility." ;
    cof:pageNumber "156"^^xsd:integer .

