doc:sch-4-sec-55zb-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "55ZB(1) Evidence by Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security—" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Before determining that a document is not an exempt document under section 33, the Information Commissioner must request the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security to appear personally and give evidence on: (a) the damage that would, or could reasonably be expected to, be caused to: (i) the security of the Commonwealth; or (ii) the defence of the Commonwealth; or (iii) the international relations of the Commonwealth;   Review by Information Commissioner  Part VII Evidence by Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security  Division 9 Section 55ZB Freedom of Information Act 1982 Compilation date: 01/01/2026 if access to the document were given in accordance with the request; or (b) whether giving access to the document in accordance with the request would divulge any information or matter communicated in confidence by, or on behalf of, a foreign government, an authority of a foreign government or an international organisation to the Government of the Commonwealth, to an authority of the Commonwealth or to a person receiving the communication on behalf of the Commonwealth or of an authority of the Commonwealth." ;
    cof:pageNumber "158"^^xsd:integer .

concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55zb-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "55ZB(2) Evidence by Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security—"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-55zb-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Before determining that an agency or Minister must grant access to a copy of the document with deletions, the Information Commissioner must request the Inspector-General to appear personally and give evidence on: (a) the damage that would, or could reasonably be expected to, be caused to: (i) the security of the Commonwealth; or (ii) the defence of the Commonwealth; or (iii) the international relations of the Commonwealth; if the proposed deletions were not made; or (b) whether giving access to the document without the proposed deletions would divulge any information or matter communicated in confidence by, or on behalf of, a foreign government, an authority of a foreign government or an international organisation to the Government of the Commonwealth, to an authority of the Commonwealth or to a person receiving the communication on behalf of the Commonwealth or of an authority of the Commonwealth." ;
    skos:definition "(2) Before determining that an agency or Minister must grant access to a copy of the document with deletions, the Information Commissioner must request the Inspector-General to appear personally and give evidence on: (a) the damage that would, or could reasonably be expected to, be caused to: (i) the security of the Commonwealth; or (ii) the defence of the Commonwealth; or (iii) the international relations of the Commonwealth; if the proposed deletions were not made; or (b) whether giving access to the document without the proposed deletions would divulge any information or matter communicated in confidence by, or on behalf of, a foreign government, an authority of a foreign government or an international organisation to the Government of the Commonwealth, to an authority of the Commonwealth or to a person receiving the communication on behalf of the Commonwealth or of an authority of the Commonwealth."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4e030b7e7056f276daaffa6a1920cbc57f81a19aae28cb809622ce162d59e1cc" ;
    values:partOf concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-55zb ;
    cof:pageNumber "158"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Request for Inspector-General to appear and give evidence on potential damage or divulgence of confidential information." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
