    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-60a-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Before determining that the document is not an exempt document under section 33, the Tribunal must request the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security to appear personally and give evidence on: (a) the damage that would, or could reasonably be expected to, be caused to: (i) the security of the Commonwealth; or (ii) the defence of the Commonwealth; or (iii) the international relations of the Commonwealth; if access to the document were given in accordance with the request; or (b) whether giving access to the document in accordance with the request would divulge any information or matter communicated in confidence by or on behalf of a foreign government, an authority of a foreign government or an international organisation to the Government of the Commonwealth, to an authority of the Commonwealth or to a" ;
    skos:definition "(2) Before determining that the document is not an exempt document under section 33, the Tribunal must request the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security to appear personally and give evidence on: (a) the damage that would, or could reasonably be expected to, be caused to: (i) the security of the Commonwealth; or (ii) the defence of the Commonwealth; or (iii) the international relations of the Commonwealth; if access to the document were given in accordance with the request; or (b) whether giving access to the document in accordance with the request would divulge any information or matter communicated in confidence by or on behalf of a foreign government, an authority of a foreign government or an international organisation to the Government of the Commonwealth, to an authority of the Commonwealth or to a"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "404d8c803024660b72e4d00ac7cb5a4db9976b412d880611c2c7b4044aa54a87" ;
    values:partOf concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-60a ;
    cof:pageNumber "173"^^xsd:integer ;
