doc:sch-4-sec-66-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "66(1) Tribunal may make recommendation that costs be available in" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Where: (a) a person applies, under section 57A, to the Tribunal for review of a decision of the Information Commissioner on an IC review; and (b) the person is successful, or substantially successful, in his or her application for review; the Tribunal may, in its discretion, recommend to the responsible Minister that the costs of the applicant in relation to the proceedings be paid by the Commonwealth." ;
    cof:pageNumber "184"^^xsd:integer .

concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-66-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "66(2) Tribunal may make recommendation that costs be available in"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-66-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Without limiting the generality of the matters to which the Tribunal may have regard in deciding whether to make a recommendation under subsection (1), the Tribunal shall have regard to: (a) the question whether payment of the costs or any part of the costs would cause financial hardship to the applicant; (b) the question whether the decision of the Tribunal on review will be of benefit to the general public; (c) the question whether the decision of the Tribunal on review will be of commercial benefit to the person making application to the Tribunal; and (d) the reasonableness of the decision reviewed by the Tribunal." ;
    skos:definition "(2) Without limiting the generality of the matters to which the Tribunal may have regard in deciding whether to make a recommendation under subsection (1), the Tribunal shall have regard to: (a) the question whether payment of the costs or any part of the costs would cause financial hardship to the applicant; (b) the question whether the decision of the Tribunal on review will be of benefit to the general public; (c) the question whether the decision of the Tribunal on review will be of commercial benefit to the person making application to the Tribunal; and (d) the reasonableness of the decision reviewed by the Tribunal."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6acc5d5f3813676b8264f7c70e989f15939d8ef3a6398094cacb75fedb454d0f" ;
    values:partOf concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-66 ;
    cof:pageNumber "184"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Tribunal must consider financial hardship, public benefit, commercial benefit, and decision reasonableness when making a recommendation." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
