doc:sch-4-sec-68 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "68 Investigations and complaints—guide" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "This Part is about investigations by the Information Commissioner and by the Ombudsman. Division 2 sets up a system for investigations by the Information Commissioner. The Information Commissioner may investigate an action taken by an agency in the performance of functions or the exercise of powers under this Act on a complaint from a person, or on the Information Commissioner’s initiative. If a person disputes the merits of an access refusal decision or an access grant decision, this Act provides elsewhere for the review of that decision (see Parts VI, VII and VIIA). However, this does not prevent a person from making a complaint to the Information Commissioner about the way in which the agency has handled the decision. The Information Commissioner has powers to obtain documents, to question persons and to enter premises (see Subdivision D of" ;
    cof:pageNumber "187"^^xsd:integer .

concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-69 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "69 Information Commissioner investigations—power to investigate"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-69 ;
    values:originalText "Obligation to investigate (1) The Information Commissioner must, subject to this Division, investigate a complaint made under section 70. Discretion to investigate (2) The Information Commissioner may, at the Information Commissioner’s initiative, investigate an action taken by an agency (the respondent agency) in the performance of functions, or the exercise of powers, under this Act. Subdivision B—Making complaints" ;
    skos:definition "Obligation to investigate (1) The Information Commissioner must, subject to this Division, investigate a complaint made under section 70. Discretion to investigate (2) The Information Commissioner may, at the Information Commissioner’s initiative, investigate an action taken by an agency (the respondent agency) in the performance of functions, or the exercise of powers, under this Act. Subdivision B—Making complaints"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7848baba34a3d7404c916a3169e00438277976a870ec19ca6bab3ce5a2661c60" ;
    cof:pageNumber "189"^^xsd:integer ;
