concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-77-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "77(6) Information Commissioner investigations—general power to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-77-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) An authorised person is: (a) an information officer (within the meaning of the Australian Information Commissioner Act 2010); or (b) an APS employee who: (i) is performing the duties of an Executive Level 2, or equivalent, position (or a higher position) in the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner; and (ii) is authorised by the Information Commissioner for the purposes of this section." ;
    skos:definition "(6) An authorised person is: (a) an information officer (within the meaning of the Australian Information Commissioner Act 2010); or (b) an APS employee who: (i) is performing the duties of an Executive Level 2, or equivalent, position (or a higher position) in the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner; and (ii) is authorised by the Information Commissioner for the purposes of this section."@en ;
