    skos:definition "(5) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person is subject to a requirement specified in a notice under subsection (3); and (b) the person engages in conduct; and (c) the person’s conduct breaches the requirement. Penalty for a contravention of this subsection: Imprisonment for 6 months. Note: Chapter 2 of the Criminal Code sets out the general principles of criminal responsibility."@en ;
