doc:sch-4-sec-89l a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "89L Vexatious applicants—grounds for declaration" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Information Commissioner may make a vexatious applicant declaration in relation to a person only if the Information Commissioner is satisfied of any of the following: (a) that: (i) the person has repeatedly engaged in access actions; and (ii) the repeated engagement involves an abuse of the process for the access action;" ;
    cof:pageNumber "209"^^xsd:integer .

concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-89m a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "89M Vexatious applicants—effect of declaration"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-89m ;
    values:originalText "(1) A vexatious applicant declaration has effect in accordance with the terms and conditions stated in the declaration. (2) Without limiting subsection (1), a vexatious applicant declaration in relation to a person may provide that: (a) an agency or Minister may refuse to consider any of the following if made by the person without the written permission of the Information Commissioner:   Miscellaneous  Part VIII Vexatious applicants  Division 1 Section 89N Freedom of Information Act 1982 Compilation date: 01/01/2026 (i) a request; (ii) an application under section 48 (amendment of records); (iii) an application for internal review; and (b) the Information Commissioner may refuse to consider an IC review application made by the person. (3) If a decision is made as mentioned in subsection (2), the agency, Minister or the Information Commissioner (as the case requires) must, as soon as practicable, notify the vexatious applicant of the decision." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A vexatious applicant declaration has effect in accordance with the terms and conditions stated in the declaration. (2) Without limiting subsection (1), a vexatious applicant declaration in relation to a person may provide that: (a) an agency or Minister may refuse to consider any of the following if made by the person without the written permission of the Information Commissioner:   Miscellaneous  Part VIII Vexatious applicants  Division 1 Section 89N Freedom of Information Act 1982 Compilation date: 01/01/2026 (i) a request; (ii) an application under section 48 (amendment of records); (iii) an application for internal review; and (b) the Information Commissioner may refuse to consider an IC review application made by the person. (3) If a decision is made as mentioned in subsection (2), the agency, Minister or the Information Commissioner (as the case requires) must, as soon as practicable, notify the vexatious applicant of the decision."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e82d11ac9d41eb67a05f2b0bddede015eb80c9ae166bc85b242a321076c6f4eb" ;
    cof:pageNumber "210"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-89m-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-89m-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-89m-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf> ;
    dc:source "freedom-of-information-act-1982.pdf, p.210" .
doc:sch-4-sec-89m a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "89M Vexatious applicants—effect of declaration" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A vexatious applicant declaration has effect in accordance with the terms and conditions stated in the declaration. (2) Without limiting subsection (1), a vexatious applicant declaration in relation to a person may provide that: (a) an agency or Minister may refuse to consider any of the following if made by the person without the written permission of the Information Commissioner:   Miscellaneous  Part VIII Vexatious applicants  Division 1 Section 89N Freedom of Information Act 1982 Compilation date: 01/01/2026 (i) a request; (ii) an application under section 48 (amendment of records); (iii) an application for internal review; and (b) the Information Commissioner may refuse to consider an IC review application made by the person. (3) If a decision is made as mentioned in subsection (2), the agency, Minister or the Information Commissioner (as the case requires) must, as soon as practicable, notify the vexatious applicant of the decision." ;
    cof:pageNumber "210"^^xsd:integer .

