concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-89m-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "89M(2) Vexatious applicants—effect of declaration"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-89m-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), a vexatious applicant declaration in relation to a person may provide that: (a) an agency or Minister may refuse to consider any of the following if made by the person without the written permission of the Information Commissioner:   Miscellaneous  Part VIII Vexatious applicants  Division 1 Section 89N Freedom of Information Act 1982 Compilation date: 01/01/2026 (i) a request; (ii) an application under section 48 (amendment of records); (iii) an application for internal review; and (b) the Information Commissioner may refuse to consider an IC review application made by the person." ;
    skos:definition "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), a vexatious applicant declaration in relation to a person may provide that: (a) an agency or Minister may refuse to consider any of the following if made by the person without the written permission of the Information Commissioner:   Miscellaneous  Part VIII Vexatious applicants  Division 1 Section 89N Freedom of Information Act 1982 Compilation date: 01/01/2026 (i) a request; (ii) an application under section 48 (amendment of records); (iii) an application for internal review; and (b) the Information Commissioner may refuse to consider an IC review application made by the person."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e6be115d81c81d28dec3edc89f25e08e4bcc157819e146e99fb6bc3fa24e0346" ;
    values:partOf concept:freedom-of-information-act-1982-sch-4-sec-89m ;
    cof:pageNumber "210"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Refusal to consider certain requests or applications without written permission." ;
